{"base_rate":0.38501971090670173,"brier":0.11876964520367937,"bss":0.4983956440885622,"bss_hi":0.575252273239002,"bss_lo":0.41515445556746056,"chart":{"base":[561.2,101.6],"fp":[232.3,293.0],"lead":"62,229.4 272,204.3 482,160.8 692,101.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.50 — higher than 88% of cities","fp":"low end +4pp, high end +11pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 29% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 2%; promised 99% → rained 88%"},"rel":"63.6,456 195.5,334.2 535.5,177 686.6,86.7"},"country":"CH","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.06689881734559791,"ess":390.7145388500043,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Basel</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Basel rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>88%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nBASEL BINNINGEN, 2.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.50, ranked 16 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(6&ndash;35) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>301</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>63%</td><td class='num'><b>60%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>88%</b></td><td class='num'>164</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Basel</b> <span class=\"muted\">CH</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.50</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>6&ndash;35\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Basel &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Basel\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.91734219269103,378.3720930232558 94.31948051948052,315.8181818181818 171.69376623376627,226.0 282.37780821917806,112.7397260273973 368.18608695652176,39.10144927536231 408.9564634146342,18.0 408.9564634146342,26.878048780487802 368.18608695652176,91.85507246376812 282.37780821917806,192.5205479452055 171.69376623376627,301.6363636363636 94.31948051948052,367.8181818181818 58.91734219269103,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"241.85282522996056\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"241.85282522996056\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.91734219269103,373.5348837209302 94.31948051948052,306.3636363636364 171.69376623376627,235.45454545454544 282.37780821917806,162.6027397260274 368.18608695652176,112.95652173913044 408.9564634146342,62.39024390243901\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 301 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.91734219269103\" cy=\"373.5348837209302\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 10%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"94.31948051948052\" cy=\"306.3636363636364\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 32%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"171.69376623376627\" cy=\"235.45454545454544\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 63%&amp;#10;It rained 60% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"282.37780821917806\" cy=\"162.6027397260274\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"368.18608695652176\" cy=\"112.95652173913044\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 88% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 164 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"408.9564634146342\" cy=\"62.39024390243901\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(39%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Basel the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.59) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.40).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>183</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.404</td><td class='num'>6.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>0.461</td><td class='num'>8.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.499</td><td class='num'>4.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.594</td><td class='num'>5.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":47.55839,"lon":7.57327,"n":761,"n_cities":134,"name":"Basel","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.002591362126245847,"n":301,"obs":0.023255813953488372,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.1025974025974026,"n":77,"obs":0.2077922077922078,"sig":true},{"hi":0.5,"lo":0.2,"